NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
MONGODB_DBNAME=teammatchup
TEST_MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
TEST_MONGODB_DBNAME=teammatchup_test
# Development value, NOT a secret: it works in development and test; in production the server
# refuses to start with it. For production, generate your own: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=solo-desarrollo-no-usar-en-produccion
# Optional: listening address (e.g. 0.0.0.0 on the course server).
# Empty or commented out: listens on all interfaces.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# On the course server (see "Deployment" in README.md) the .env is created by hand there,
# never uploaded, and changes these values:
#   NODE_ENV=production
#   PORT=7041
#   HOST=0.0.0.0
#   MONGODB_URI=<course-mongodb-uri>/?authSource=admin
#   MONGODB_DBNAME=fullstack      (no permission for a database of our own; collections use tmu_)
#   JWT_SECRET=<generated with openssl rand -hex 32>
#   PUBLIC_URL=https://fullstack.dcc.uchile.cl:7041   (only if STEAM_API_KEY is set)
# Optional (verify the CS2 account with Steam). Without STEAM_API_KEY, Steam verification is not
# offered and everything else works the same.
# Steam Web API key (https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey): it is a secret, it goes only in
# each instance's .env and is never committed to the repository.
# STEAM_API_KEY=
# Address the browser uses to open this instance (no path or trailing slash); Steam sends the
# user back here. Required if there is a key; in production it must be https. Examples:
#   local development (Vite): http://localhost:5173
#   course server:            https://fullstack.dcc.uchile.cl:7041
# PUBLIC_URL=
# Optional (verify the League of Legends account with Riot Games). Without RIOT_API_KEY,
# Riot Games verification is not offered and everything else works the same (does not need PUBLIC_URL).
# Riot Games development key (https://developer.riotgames.com/): it expires every 24 hours and is
# renewed by hand by replacing it in the .env and restarting the server. It is a secret, it goes
# only in each instance's .env and is never committed to the repository.
# RIOT_API_KEY=
# Optional (real CS2 Premier rating from Leetify). Without LEETIFY_API_KEY requests are still made,
# with Leetify's lower limits; it does not need PUBLIC_URL.
# Leetify public API key (https://leetify.com/app/developer): it is a secret, it goes only in
# each instance's .env and is never committed to the repository.
# LEETIFY_API_KEY=
